 "final": "I set up the spec and checked it: it validates with no findings, and every pad and the base select nodes (121 nodes per pad, 10,201 on the base). In the render the bottom face (z = 0) is shown fixed and the four pads sit on the top face (z = 100). The render draws y as the vertical axis, so the view looks rotated, but the coordinates are right.\n\n**Setup:**\n- **Domain and settings:** 100 \u00d7 100 \u00d7 100 mm, steel (E 210,000 N/mm\u00b2, \u03bd 0.3), volume fraction 0.15, 1 mm elements (1,000,000 elements).\n- **Support:** the whole z = 0 face is fixed in x, y and z.\n- **Loads:** four 10 \u00d7 10 mm pads on the top face, each flush with its edge and centred on the edge midpoint. Each carries 100 N along its edge:\n\n| Pad | Location | Force |\n|---|---|---|\n| South | x 45\u201355, y 0\u201310 | +x |\n| East | x 90\u2013100, y 45\u201355 | +y |\n| North | x 45\u201355, y 90\u2013100 | \u2212x |\n| West | x 0\u201310, y 45\u201355 | \u2212y |\n\nThese directions give a counter-clockwise torque about +z, seen from above.\n\nDONE. Assumptions:\n- **Force per pad:** each pad's force acts at the pad centre, 45 mm from the vertical axis. That gives 100 N per pad (4 \u00d7 100 N \u00d7 45 mm = 18 N\u00b7m). If you measure the lever arm to the edge instead (50 mm), it would be 90 N per pad.\n- **Spread over the pad:** each pad's force is shared equally by the pad's top-face nodes.\n- **No keep-solid zones:** the brief doesn't mention any, so the pads and base have no forced solid material.",
